==Description==

The [[Image:Silk_ControlPoly4_segment.svg|32px]] '''Silk PControlPoly4 segment''' command creates a 4 node control polygon, a ControlPoly4_segment object, for a segment of a CubicCurve_4, between two points on the curve.

</translate>
[[File:4.-ControlPoly4_segment.png|300px]]
<translate>

{{Caption|Segmented ControlPoly4´s.}}

==Usage==

# Preselect in the [[Tree_View|Tree View]] :
## A [[Silk_ControlPoly4|ControlPoly4]] curve.
## The first [[Silk_Point_onCurve|Point]] on the curve.
## The second [[Silk_Point_onCurve|Point]] on the curve.
# There are several ways to invoke the tool.
#* Press the {{Button|[[Image:Silk_ControlPoly4_segment.svg|16px]] ControlPoly4_segment}} button.
#* Select the {{MenuCommand|[[Image:Silk_ControlPoly4_segment.svg|16px]] Silk → ControlPoly4_segment}} option from the menu.
# A '''ControlPoly4_segment''' object is created.

== Properties ==

See also: [[Property_View|Property View]].

A  '''ControlPoly4_segment''' is derived from a [[Part_Feature|Part feature]], or more precise a {{Incode|Part::FeaturePython}} object, and inherits all its properties. It also has the following additional properties:

=== Data ===

{{Properties_Title|C1 - Inputs}}

* {{PropertyData|NL_Curve|Link}}: Reference curve.
* {{PropertyData|Point_onCurve_0|Link}}: Segment start point.
* {{PropertyData|Point_onCurve_1|Link}}: Segment end point.
* {{PropertyData|reverse|Bool}}: Default is {{value|False}}. Reverses the parameter direction.

{{Properties_Title|C2 - Outputs}}

* {{PropertyData|Legs|Part::PropertyGeometryList}}: Control segments.
* {{PropertyData|Poles|VectorList}}: Poles.
* {{PropertyData|Weights|FloatList}}: Weights.

{{Properties_Title|C3 - Identifiers}}

* {{PropertyData|internalName|String}}: The permanent internal FreeCAD name for this object.
* {{PropertyData|object_type|String}}: Default is {{value|ControlPoly4_segment}}. The workbench class used to create this object.
* {{PropertyData|object_version|String}}: The class version of this object.


